(1791971, 244726, 16053, '<td valign="top">Very good flare control from your lens! Good photo with nice saturated colors.</td>', 'Very good flare control from your lens! Good photo with nice saturated colors.', '2005-10-18 04:45:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(1791972, 244803, 16053, '<td valign="top">I love the contrast between the blue sky and the browns and greens from the plants.</td>', 'I love the contrast between the blue sky and the browns and greens from the plants.', '2005-10-18 04:46:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(1791977, 243795, 16053, '<td valign="top">Not so wide but an excellent photo. A winner for shure.</td>', 'Not so wide but an excellent photo. A winner for shure.', '2005-10-18 04:52:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(1791979, 242864, 16053, '<td valign="top">Very interesting point of view, and tipe of fisheye image. Good color combination.</td>', 'Very interesting point of view, and tipe of fisheye image. Good color combination.', '2005-10-18 04:53:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(1791980, 245100, 24784, '<td valign="top">great idea</td>', 'great idea', '2005-10-18 04:53:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(1791982, 244677, 16053, '<td valign="top">Excellent color cast of the sunset. Very good mood. My favorite.</td>', 'Excellent color cast of the sunset. Very good mood. My favorite.', '2005-10-18 04:54:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(1791989, 245085, 16053, '<td valign="top">I love the tiled horizon. It ads a lot ot the image, to the different pespective. Thes sun was a bit high I think and might have condicioned the colors and heavy shadows. If the glass was a bit more green and the sky did''nt have those plots that looks like sensor dust it was a 10 for me. An 8 this way. just a hint: in photosho if you select only the grass with for example the magic wand tool and you copy it as a new layer then you can put the blending options in "dodge"  and play with opacity to brighten the grass slectively. Play with the opacity so you don''t get a unnatural look. 40-60 % used to work well.</td>', 'I love the tiled horizon. It ads a lot ot the image, to the different pespective. Thes sun was a bit high I think and might have condicioned the colors and heavy shadows. If the glass was a bit more green and the sky did''nt have those plots that looks like sensor dust it was a 10 for me. An 8 this way. just a hint: in photosho if you select only the grass with for example the magic wand tool and you copy it as a new layer then you can put the blending options in "dodge"  and play with opacity to brighten the grass slectively. Play with the opacity so you don''t get a unnatural look. 40-60 % used to work well.', '2005-10-18 05:04:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(1792025, 244452, 41522, '<td valign="top">A wonderful tonal quality to the building.  Good use of the wide angle to create the perspective shot.  I''m impressed with the focus and clarity  of the building lines as my eye moves upward along the building.  My only nit would be the little nit of grey cloud along the left side near the top.  A minor distraction at most.  Excellent photo.</td>', 'A wonderful tonal quality to the building.  Good use of the wide angle to create the perspective shot.  I''m impressed with the focus and clarity  of the building lines as my eye moves upward along the building.  My only nit would be the little nit of grey cloud along the left side near the top.  A minor distraction at most.  Excellent photo.', '2005-10-18 06:13:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(1792033, 243153, 41522, '<td valign="top">A wonderful image.  Nice sharp silhouette.  Awesome composition (a nice rule of thirds rule breaker!)  Wonderful colours.  My only nit is the flash of colour at the bottom left corner.  Because it is so different from the rest of the image, it stands out very much and as such, is a bit distracting to me.  Overall, a very good job.</td>', 'A wonderful image.  Nice sharp silhouette.  Awesome composition (a nice rule of thirds rule breaker!)  Wonderful colours.  My only nit is the flash of colour at the bottom left corner.  Because it is so different from the rest of the image, it stands out very much and as such, is a bit distracting to me.  Overall, a very good job.', '2005-10-18 06:20:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(1792036, 244338, 41522, '<td valign="top">Nice work on this image.  Overall, a good composition and the symmetry is really pleasing to look at, IMO.  I like the B&amp;W for this shot.  Good eye.</td>', 'Nice work on this image.  Overall, a good composition and the symmetry is really pleasing to look at, IMO.  I like the B&W for this shot.  Good eye.', '2005-10-18 06:22:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(1792042, 243157, 41522, '<td valign="top">I can see that you''ve used a wide angle with the and the sunrise colours in the centre are well exposed.  For me, the composition is a little too centred for my liking and the foreground is too dark.  I''m not sure if you used any filters on this to help with the exposure control, but I would have liked the forground to have been a little lighter to emhasize the depth of the wide angle.  JMO.</td>', 'I can see that you''ve used a wide angle with the and the sunrise colours in the centre are well exposed.  For me, the composition is a little too centred for my liking and the foreground is too dark.  I''m not sure if you used any filters on this to help with the exposure control, but I would have liked the forground to have been a little lighter to emhasize the depth of the wide angle.  JMO.', '2005-10-18 06:26:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(1792048, 244174, 16053, '<td valign="top">Excellent lightning and use of backlight. 8</td>', 'Excellent lightning and use of backlight. 8', '2005-10-18 06:35:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(1792049, 245148, 41522, '<td valign="top">The wide angle usage is evident.  The shot is nice, but I was wondering if you tried other perspectives of this shot, such as a different placement of the horizon or even placing the cmera really close to the ground and offering a little more foreground.  Just curious.</td>', 'The wide angle usage is evident.  The shot is nice, but I was wondering if you tried other perspectives of this shot, such as a different placement of the horizon or even placing the cmera really close to the ground and offering a little more foreground.  Just curious.', '2005-10-18 06:35:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(1792052, 244981, 16053, '<td valign="top">Good photo, I would like to see it in color though, and with a slower shutter speed in order to blur more the waterfalls</td>', 'Good photo, I would like to see it in color though, and with a slower shutter speed in order to blur more the waterfalls', '2005-10-18 06:37:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(1792053, 244916, 33352, '<td valign="top">no need for words...10</td>', 'no need for words...10', '2005-10-18 06:37:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(1792055, 245037, 16053, '<td valign="top">Here''s one that put a smile on me. good to see.</td>', 'Here''s one that put a smile on me. good to see.', '2005-10-18 06:38:29.000000', NULL, 1),
