(1817042, 244193, 41802, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>Ok wow, after reading your description and seeing this was a standard 18-55mm that''s just crazy. What an amazing find to see building that actually curve like that.  The coloring of the building is a great force to have in this shot. the lighting really draws attention to the curves, I was wondering what it looked like in real life when I saw this in the challenge.  Personally I scored you higher then you placed. I think between your angle and lighting the placement should have been higher. Great include of the street name to draw attentions to your nice lines in the image. I think your contrast also helps enhances the buildings themselves.</td>', '*Critique Club* Ok wow, after reading your description and seeing this was a standard 18-55mm that''s just crazy. What an amazing find to see building that actually curve like that.  The coloring of the building is a great force to have in this shot. the lighting really draws attention to the curves, I was wondering what it looked like in real life when I saw this in the challenge.  Personally I scored you higher then you placed. I think between your angle and lighting the placement should have been higher. Great include of the street name to draw attentions to your nice lines in the image. I think your contrast also helps enhances the buildings themselves.', '2005-10-27 01:43:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(1817059, 245164, 41802, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>This shot defiantly sticks out in my head from the challenge.  Maybe its me but the image feels a little leaning.  Awesome attempt at a night shot, I myself have not been nearly as brave.  I love the water on the ground, I am glad you chose to go with the rainy day instead of just regular. The light seem a little too over the top maybe a little over exposed.  I think it is such a different thought then the basic landscape that we knew would fill the challenge. The image really looks like there are tress branches off the the right side that take way from the glow of the lights.  Good attempt!</td>', '*Critique Club* This shot defiantly sticks out in my head from the challenge.  Maybe its me but the image feels a little leaning.  Awesome attempt at a night shot, I myself have not been nearly as brave.  I love the water on the ground, I am glad you chose to go with the rainy day instead of just regular. The light seem a little too over the top maybe a little over exposed.  I think it is such a different thought then the basic landscape that we knew would fill the challenge. The image really looks like there are tress branches off the the right side that take way from the glow of the lights.  Good attempt!', '2005-10-27 01:55:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(1817068, 244673, 41802, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/> <br/>Personally I like the shot.   It is a rare shot to get all the placement just right for something like this, with the moon, the glow, the man and the height.  I think it would have been hard to title this one, but voters seem critical of things like that.  Personally I scored you higher and I think other should have too.  I like the subject is looking up as opposed to the typical downward depression. I think if you cropped this image tighter you would have lost some of the effect between the moon and structure.  I think the shot maybe we have scored a little higher with a softer shot then with the harder noise.  But I think you did an excellent job.</td>', '*Critique Club* Personally I like the shot.   It is a rare shot to get all the placement just right for something like this, with the moon, the glow, the man and the height.  I think it would have been hard to title this one, but voters seem critical of things like that.  Personally I scored you higher and I think other should have too.  I like the subject is looking up as opposed to the typical downward depression. I think if you cropped this image tighter you would have lost some of the effect between the moon and structure.  I think the shot maybe we have scored a little higher with a softer shot then with the harder noise.  But I think you did an excellent job.', '2005-10-27 02:00:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(1817299, 245095, 29658, '<td valign="top">It''s one of those shots that make you think... and one of those that renew the joy of taking pictures to tell a story. First place for me.<br/> <br/>S.</td>', 'It''s one of those shots that make you think... and one of those that renew the joy of taking pictures to tell a story. First place for me. S.', '2005-10-27 07:04:23.000000', NULL, 0),
